This AI-powered assistant helps universities benchmark peer and aspirational institution policies, distinguish majority from minority frameworks
with precise, traceable citations, and draft robust institutional policies built on your own templates and writing standards. Purpose-built for
sponsored programs and compliance work, it screens every draft against core federal frameworks (i.e., 2 CFR Part 200 (Uniform Guidance), the FAR, 
and NSF/NIH terms) and keeps a qualified administrator in control at every step through a structured, human-in-the-loop workflow. Grounded strictly
in the policy documents you provide to minimize hallucination, it turns hours of comparative analysis into a clear, decision-ready draft, so your
team can move from research to reliable policy, faster.

The system instructions are AI tool agnostic, so you can easily implement them into your preferred platform, including:

Gemini (Gems)
Claude (Projects)
ChatGPT (GPTs)
Microsoft Copilot (Agents)
Any in-house AI Assistants or Agents

Getting started requires minimal setup and zero coding experience. Simply copy and paste our comprehensive system instructions into your AI tool
and upload your institution's relevant policy-writing guidelines.


